# What goes into the image. Everything else stays in the project folder (nothing is deleted); it is just not
# copied in: .env and other secrets, customer data (data/escalations, data/kb_research), local models (.tools),
# research, chat exports, tests and the dashboard's source and node_modules.
*
!requirements.txt
!config.py
!notifier/
!dashboard/
dashboard/web/
!kb/
!config/
!data/Roster_*.csv
!docker/
!scripts/check_slack.py
**/__pycache__
# Emergent farm template build inputs: these MUST reach the build context or every template COPY fails
# (COPY backend/, frontend/, nginx.conf, entrypoint.sh, pip-cache/...). Do not remove these re-includes.
!backend/
!frontend/
!nginx.conf
!entrypoint.sh
!pip-cache/
# ...but still keep generated/vendored junk out of the (now re-included) frontend/.
frontend/node_modules/
